  77:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c **** 
  78:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c **** /*
  79:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * The core arithmetic decoding routine (common in JPEG and JBIG).
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccRJf3no.s 			page 4


  80:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * This needs to go as fast as possible.
  81:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * Machine-dependent optimization facilities
  82:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * are not utilized in this portable implementation.
  83:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * However, this code should be fairly efficient and
  84:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * may be a good base for further optimizations anyway.
  85:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  *
  86:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * Return value is 0 or 1 (binary decision).
  87:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  *
  88:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * Note: I've changed the handling of the code base & bit
  89:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * buffer register C compared to other implementations
  90:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * based on the standards layout & procedures.
  91:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * While it also contains both the actual base of the
  92:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * coding interval (16 bits) and the next-bits buffer,
  93:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * the cut-point between these two parts is floating
  94:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * (instead of fixed) with the bit shift counter CT.
  95:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * Thus, we also need only one (variable instead of
  96:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * fixed size) shift for the LPS/MPS decision, and
  97:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * we can get away with any renormalization update
  98:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * of C (except for new data insertion, of course).
  99:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  *
 100:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * I've also introduced a new scheme for accessing
 101:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * the probability estimation state machine table,
 102:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  * derived from Markus Kuhn's JBIG implementation.
 103:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c ****  */
 104:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jdarith.c **** 
